Hugo Presentation Demohttps://tgehr.github.io/rubberduq26/presentations/demo/Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000https://tgehr.github.io/rubberduq26/presentations/demo/<h1 id="slides-from-one-markdown-file">Slides from one Markdown file</h1>
<p>Hugo + KaTeX + the existing plotting shortcodes</p>
<hr>
<h1 id="mathematics-with-katex">Mathematics with KaTeX</h1>
<p>Inline math stays inline: eiπ+1=0.</p>
<p>Display math is centered and typeset during postprocessing:</p>
<p>∫−∞∞​e−x2,dx=π​</p>
<p>The same source works with sums, matrices, and aligned equations.</p>
<hr>
<h1 id="a-generated-plot">A generated plot</h1>
<p>The plot below uses the project&rsquo;s existing <code>plot</code> and <code>series</code> shortcodes.</p>
<div class="pp-plot has-explicit-size" data-plot='{&#34;hash&#34;:&#34;f7896d368bcf&#34;,&#34;plot&#34;:{&#34;grid&#34;:&#34;true&#34;,&#34;height&#34;:&#34;400&#34;,&#34;width&#34;:&#34;900&#34;,&#34;xmax&#34;:&#34;3.2&#34;,&#34;xmin&#34;:&#34;-3.2&#34;,&#34;ymax&#34;:&#34;1.25&#34;,&#34;ymin&#34;:&#34;-1.25&#34;},&#34;primitives&#34;:[],&#34;series&#34;:[{&#34;fn&#34;:&#34;sin(x)&#34;,&#34;samples&#34;:&#34;320&#34;,&#34;stroke&#34;:&#34;#8ab4f8&#34;},{&#34;dash&#34;:&#34;8 5&#34;,&#34;fn&#34;:&#34;cos(x)&#34;,&#34;samples&#34;:&#34;320&#34;,&#34;stroke&#34;:&#34;#2fbf71&#34;}],&#34;sliders&#34;:{},&#34;vars&#34;:{}}' style="--pp-plot-width:900px;--pp-plot-aspect:900/400;width:min(100%,var(--pp-plot-width));">
 <div class="pp-plot-embed">
 <img class="pp-plot-fallback"
 src="https://tgehr.github.io/rubberduq26/plots/f7896d368bcf.svg"
 width="900" height="400"
 style="display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; aspect-ratio: 900 / 400;"
 alt="Plot">
 </div><div class="pp-plot-controls" style="display:none"></div>
</div>

<hr>
<h1 id="interactive-plotting">Interactive plotting</h1>
<p>The same shortcode system supports live parameters. Move either slider:</p>
Practical High-level Quantum Programminghttps://tgehr.github.io/rubberduq26/presentations/nvidia26/Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000https://tgehr.github.io/rubberduq26/presentations/nvidia26/<!--
Ported from the Beamer source presentation(1).tex.
